### IntelliJ HTTP Client API Tests
### Requires 'REST Client' extension in VSCode or IntelliJ IDEA natively.

@host = http://localhost:8080
@username = testuser1
@password = Password123!

### 1. Register User 1
# @name signupUser1
POST {{host}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User 1",
  "username": "{{username}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 2. Login User 1
# @name loginUser1
POST {{host}}/auth/signin
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{username}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("token1", response.body.data.token);
%}

### 3. Get User 1 Profile
GET {{host}}/profile/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token1}}

### 4. Create a Thought
# @name createThought
POST {{host}}/thoughts/
Authorization: Bearer {{token1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "This is my first thought on the platform!"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("thoughtId", response.body.data.thoughtId);
%}

### 5. Get the created Thought
GET {{host}}/thoughts/{{thoughtId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token1}}

### 6. Like the Thought
GET {{host}}/thoughts/interact/{{thoughtId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token1}}

### 7. Get Thought Likes
GET {{host}}/thoughts/likes/{{thoughtId}}?limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token1}}

### 8. Search Users
GET {{host}}/profile/search/testuser
Authorization: Bearer {{token1}}

### 9. Create an Opinion (Reply) on the Thought
POST {{host}}/thoughts/
Authorization: Bearer {{token1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "This is an opinion replying to the first thought.",
  "parentThoughtId": {{thoughtId}}
}

### 10. Get Opinions for the Thought
GET {{host}}/thoughts/opinions/{{thoughtId}}?limit=5
Authorization: Bearer {{token1}}

### 11. Update Profile (Multipart - requires proper IDE file setup, skipping raw text test here but format shown)
# PATCH {{host}}/profile/
# Authorization: Bearer {{token1}}
# Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary
#
# --boundary
# Content-Disposition: form-data; name="data"
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# {
#   "bio": "Updated bio via tests!"
# }
